From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:24:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): retire refused parent identities without retry
 fanout [daveey]

Problem: PR3913's first review correction kept a permanently refused synthetic
parent under one cached op ID forever, and new child rows during materialized
parent backoff synthesized competing full-row retries.

Why1: permanent rejection preserved the uncertain-send envelope even though the
server returned a definitive verdict; Worker applied_ops recalls that rejection.
Why2: _unacked_parents counted only selected parent rows, not pending backoff rows.
Root(happened): uncertain transport custody was conflated with definitive refusal,
and pending retry ownership was scoped to the current batch instead of the outbox.
Root(not caught): the original eight-round fake did not cache rejection receipts
and did not add children while the parent retry was in backoff.
Recurrence: corrections to reviewer6004212104 were incomplete; re-review
6004316360/6004319562 supplied the missing behavior probes.

Countermeasures:
- retire any definitively refused synthetic envelope without growing rejected
  parent rows or diagnostic children; keep uncertain retries immutable.
- pending task retries suppress duplicate parent synthesis even while backed off.
- receipt-caching recovery and new-child/backoff tests: RED3 on a92a1edb68;
  GREEN797 in 11 focused files after correction, full21 check suite GREEN.

Known OPEN review finding3: immutable retry can carry stale wake status after a
completion arrives. Altering its payload conflicts with the agreed exact-byte
contract; authoritative terminal event-order arbitration needs the owning
orchestrator's source-contract disposition. This commit does not waive that
finding, approve the PR, land it, or claim overall replay safety.
